			"Message": "docs(Maintain): Rewrite Mermaid diagram to reflect full build system\n\nReplace the high-level Mermaid architecture diagram in README.md with a comprehensive breakdown of Maintain's internal modules, shell entrypoints, and build artifacts. The new diagram documents:\n\n- Source/Build/ core: CLI subcommands (build/debug/release/profile), JSON5/TOML/Plist editing, PascalCase utilities, target triple resolution\n- Build/Rhai/ subsystem: script interpreter, config loader, environment resolver, script runner\n- Source/Run/ logic: dev server launch, process management, profiling\n- Shell script entrypoints: Debug/Build.sh, Release/Build.sh, SignBundle.sh, BrotliPrebake\n- Build artifact targets: Mountain .app bundle, Cargo.toml, plist files\n\nEach node group is color-coded (maintain, script, config, artifact) using Mermaid classDefs with accessible color contrast for visual clarity.\n\nAlso fix a literal tab character in Source/Build/PlistEdit.rs, replacing it with the escaped byte `\\t` to adhere to Rust coding conventions.",
